    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d200-a1">

                <pb facs="0301" n="185" xml:id="pg185"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Hale to the
                            Minister for Foreign Affairs.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 62.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>
                            <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 30, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your excellency’s note of December 22 in reference to my
                    communication presented to His Excellency the President of the Republic on the
                    day before, and to say that your excellency has mistaken the word “request”
                    (peticién), used by me, for “insistence” (instancia) and then “demand” (demanda)
                    as used by your excellency.</p>
                <p>I have the honor further to inform your excellency that I reported the substance
                    of your excellency’s note to the Department of State, and have received the
                    answer that the representations of the Government of the United States were not
                    presented in the form of a demand, but merely as information conveyed to it and
                    transmitted by it in a spirit “of friendship and amity in the interest of peace
                    and order in Central America. Having done this much, my Government considers
                    that its responsibility ends.</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. J. Hale</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
